    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Still stucking. </p>\n<p>If this is proved, Whitehead's first lemma, Weyl's complete reducibility, Whitehead's second lemma, Levi's theorem, and Ado's theorem become axiom-free!</p>",
        "id": 629010658,
        "sender_full_name": "Miyahara Kō",
        "timestamp": 1791109266
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I suspect this is not true in the generality you have written and that you need to use the Fitting decomposition (but I have not worked it out).</p>",
        "id": 629015658,
        "sender_full_name": "Scott Carnahan",
        "timestamp": 1791110356
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>OK, I'll try it.</p>",
        "id": 629017232,
        "sender_full_name": "Miyahara Kō",
        "timestamp": 1791110613
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Finally, I couldn't prove this lemma even with Fitting assumption, so instead of using Fitting's lemma, I used quotient decomposition, and Whitehead's first lemma was proved!</p>\n<p>Now Ado's theorem is sorry free! <span aria-label=\"tada\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f389\" role=\"img\" title=\"tada\">:tada:</span></p>",
        "id": 629037685,
        "sender_full_name": "Miyahara Kō",
        "timestamp": 1791123824
    }
